WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.340
My contention is, all kids have tremendous
talents.

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:05.180
And we squander them, pretty ruthlessly.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.499
I heard a great story recently -- I love telling
it --

00:00:07.499 --> 00:00:10.019
of a little girl who was in a drawing lesson.

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:11.950
She was six, and she was at the back, drawing,

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.000
and the teacher said this girl hardly ever
paid attention,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.789
and in this drawing lesson, she did.

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:18.020
The teacher was fascinated.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.330
She went over to her, and she said, "What
are you drawing?"

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.939
And the girl said, "I'm drawing a picture
of God."

00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:25.939
And the teacher said,

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:28.310
"But nobody knows what God looks like."

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.779
And the girl said, "They will, in a minute."

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:33.520
Kids will take a chance.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.180
If they don't know, they'll have a go.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.560
Am I right?

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.450
They're not frightened of being wrong.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.050
I don't mean to say that being wrong

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.490
is the same thing as being creative.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.540
What we do know is, if you're not prepared
to be wrong,

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.890
you'll never come up with anything original
--

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.820
if you're not prepared to be wrong.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.350
And by the time they get to be adults,

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:57.330
most kids have lost that capacity.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.440
They have become frightened of being wrong.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.940
And we run our companies like this.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.330
We stigmatize mistakes.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.940
And we're now running national education systems

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.570
where mistakes are the worst thing you can
make.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.400
And the result is that we are educating people

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.040
out of their creative capacities.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.040
If you think of it,

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.590
the whole system of public education around
the world

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.750
is a protracted process of university entrance.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:20.980
And the consequence is that many highly-talented,

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.990
brilliant, creative people think they're not,

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.330
because the thing they were good at at school
wasn't valued,

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.550
or was actually stigmatized.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.540
And I think we can't afford to go on that
way.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:35.900
Picasso once said this, he said that all children
are born artists.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.210
The problem is to remain an artist as we grow
up.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.479
I believe this passionately, that we don't
grow into creativity,

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:43.729
we grow out of it.

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:46.890
Or rather, we get educated out of it.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:51.010
We have to be careful now that we use this
gift wisely,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.690
and the only way we'll do it is by seeing
our creative capacities

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.470
for the richness they are

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.350
and seeing our children for the hope that
they are.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.140
And our task is to educate their whole being,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.330
so they can face this future.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.330
By the way --

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:07.820
we may not see this future, but they will.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.690
And our job is to help them make something
of it.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:09.860
Share this video
with someone whose creativity inspires you.

